# SafeEdge — UI theming

Keep theming simple. SafeEdge does not need a multi-theme, multi-brand, or public/admin skin system initially. Do not build a full design system yet.

## Split of concerns

- **Component styles**: layout and structure (flex/grid, spacing, alignment, breakpoints, stacking).
- **Theme / tokens**: visual identity (color, gradient, shadow, radius, typography, reusable control skins).

Use CSS custom properties for reusable visual values. Do not spread hardcoded colors, shadows, radii, or fonts across many components.

```scss
// layout in the component
.candidate-list {
  display: grid;
  gap: var(--se-space-md);
}

// visual value from a token
.candidate-ev {
  color: var(--se-color-positive);
}
```

If a value is unclear (layout vs theme), put the visual part in a token.

## Reuse

Shared chrome (page shell, table surface, cards, buttons) should use tokens and shared classes, not per-screen copy-paste.

If a new color or radius is needed, add a token in the central theme stylesheet rather than hardcoding it in one component.

Light/dark can be added later via tokens. Do not invent a route-based multi-theme architecture now.

## When uncertain

Stop and ask instead of creating a second theme framework.
